       "elementos": [
        {
         "id": "e-z4hrs9",
         "tipo": "txtJustificado",
         "visible": true,
         "texto": "Biosynthetic gene clusters (BGCs) encode the pathways of specialised metabolites. antiSMASH detects them and assigns a product class with rules based on protein domains.\n\n**Questions.** What do the BGCs of *Stutzerimonas* look like in terms of Pfam domains? Is a BGC's domain profile enough to predict its class? Which domains and genes recur, and how conserved is gene order?"
        }
       ],
       "id": "b-svfg8n"
      },
      {
       "visible": true,
       "titulo": "2 · The data",
       "mostrar_titulo": true,
       "estilo": "",
